@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] v5-tenant-isolation
Storage keys and authorization MUST be tenant-scoped. Filesystem RPCs MUST derive tenant and at most
512 grants from an active session. Cached access MUST be session-scoped and expire with that session.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:concurrency;backend] v5-minimal-atomic-groups
File edits MUST use one file transaction. Create/remove MUST atomically change parent and target;
rename MUST atomically change source/destination parents, target, and replacement when present.
Independent groups MUST NOT share a transaction. Metadata, blocks, and indexes MUST stay coherent.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend;concurrency] v5-durable-server
Servers MUST acknowledge mutations only after FDB commits and MUST retain no content/metadata read
cache or writeback overlay between requests. Complete tenant permission trees MAY authorize within
their configured age bound; all other filesystem invariants MUST use current conflict-tracked FDB
state. Mutations with unknown commit outcomes MUST NOT be automatically replayed.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:concurrency] v5-object-fsync
Ordinary client mutations MAY acknowledge bounded RAM acceptance. Fsync MUST dispatch and await only
a finite prefix of the target object's edits and required namespace prerequisites, across handles.
It MUST NOT drain unrelated objects or a parent queue. Known deferred errors MUST reach fsync.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:performance;security] v5-client-freshness
Client-controlled write buffering W and read/authorization cache validity C MUST satisfy W+C<=1000ms,
initially W=200ms and C=800ms. Server/network waits are excluded. Cache validity starts at request send;
tentative new objects instead start their own C at local acceptance, without inheriting parent expiry.
Hits, edits and block fills MUST NOT renew validity. More writes MUST NOT postpone the oldest dispatch
window. RAM acceptance MAY rely on a valid child after its parent expires; the server MUST recheck
authority using one fresh-enough complete tree generation or a complete current FDB proof.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:concurrency] v5-revision-coherence
Each committed object modification MUST change its revision. Retained blocks MUST be used only with
matching freshly authorized metadata. Reads MUST NOT mix revisions or expose tails after truncation.
Client generations MUST prevent late replies from overwriting newer edits or resurrecting removals.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;concurrency] v5-directory-membership-reuse
An expired directory page MAY renew its names and child attributes together only after Validate
confirms its listing counter and authorization generation from one coherent view. Child attribute
edits MUST change the parent's listing counter without changing its public attributes/revision.
Root/shared projections MUST re-list. Local overlays and generations MUST fence late responses.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:performance] v5-bounded-client-memory
Client metadata, blocks, pages, queued/in-flight writes and bookkeeping MUST share one configured
memory budget, including reserved transient space, without a separate dirty-data cap. Admission MUST
evict clean state before waiting for memory; acknowledged dirty data MUST NOT be evicted silently.
Directory prefetch MUST be bounded by pages and bytes.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] v5-userspace-cache
FUSE MUST use direct I/O, zero metadata/name TTLs, and no kernel writeback or directory caching.
Userspace owns caching and expiry. Shared writable mmap is unsupported.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:testing] v5-commit-delay-metrics
The client's `dfs_client_metrics` MUST keep reporting, each with `max_ms`: `writeback.client_delay`
(a group's first edit accepted to dispatch), `writeback.group` (dispatch to outcome) and
`writeback.lag` (first edit accepted to outcome). x/henry/dfs-bench reads them to compare clients.
